# First Notes on String 2 (repertoire plan: st-first-notes-string-2). An original study in G
# major. Bars 1-4 stay on string 2: the open string (B), fret 1 (C) with finger 1, fret 3 (D) with
# finger 3. Bars 5-8 cross to string 1 for E (open) and G (fret 3). F from string 1 is left out:
# in G major the seventh note is F#, which comes later, and a lone F natural would need a natural
# sign against the key signature. The teacher strums G and C. It ends on B over G.
